  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 935 PM CST Tue Nov 10 2026\n\nWidespread freezes are expected both Saturday and Sunday mornings as\na large upper low/trough over the eastern CONUS slowly shifts east. A\nnegatively tilted trough axis will enter the Plains through the\nwestern Gulf of America by Sunday. The southern stream Jet will help\nto strengthen this trough over the Gulf, but also keep surface\ncyclogensis and the low track in the central Gulf. High pressure \nwill remain a dominant feature over the eastern Great Lakes and OH \nvalley. The combination of the high and low positions will maintain \nan easterly dry and cool flow across the TN valley. Only slight \ntemperature modifications will result Monday and Tuesday, with highs \nin the upper 50s to around 60, and lows in the upper 20s to lower 30s\nin southern middle TN and lower to middle 30s in north AL.",
